      "message": "Context from b/235925535:\n```\nThe header file is not the issue pointed out by Greg. I agree that binder_alloc.h is not needed, however it is where struct binder_alloc is defined so it is a good practice to use that header explicitly. The problem is that you are using a private kernel symbol, which is evident because of the line #include \u003c../drivers/android/binder_alloc.h\u003e and that\u0027s what Greg refers to. See, it\u0027s much complex to maintain and track a private definition for a stable KMI.\n```",
